4	 *
5	 * Locates a commissionable device entirely on its own — no phone-resolved
6	 * address — PASEs with the request passcode, and commissions it onto the
7	 * controller's own fabric. Two lookups run until one matches:
8	 *
9	 *  1. The controller's own SRP server table. Devices on our Thread mesh
10	 *     register their commissionable window (_matterc._udp) via SRP directly
11	 *     with us; the table has the authoritative TXT (D=<disc>) that the
12	 *     OTBR's SRP->mDNS advertising proxy strips from the local mDNS echo.
13	 *     Polled every 2 s — the window's SRP update can land moments after the
14	 *     /commission request.
15	 *  2. Commissionable DNS-SD browse (kNone + client-side discriminator match)
16	 *     for devices advertising on the LAN: Wi-Fi/Ethernet devices, and Thread
17	 *     devices proxied by another ecosystem's border router (direct handover
18	 *     of a shared pairing code).
19	 *
20	 * Device NOC signing is handled transparently by the custom credentials
21	 * issuer (flux_creds_issuer) installed in flux_bootstrap_fabric(); this file
22	 * only drives discovery + PairDevice + the pairing/commissioning delegates.
