/// Splits the controller off onto its own, freshly-generated Thread network —
/// POST /thread/split.  The inverse of [joinThreadNetwork]: the controller
/// forms a brand-new network (new network key / PAN ID / extended PAN ID) and
/// migrates its existing mesh onto it, leaving the previously-shared network
/// behind.  Devices commissioned to the controller follow the migration; the
/// other ecosystem's hubs stay on the old network.
///
/// Empty request body — there is nothing to parameterise; the controller
/// generates the credentials.  Returns the [StatusResponse] (`code == 0` on
/// success), or null on transport failure / if the controller does not
/// implement the endpoint.
Future<$proto.StatusResponse?> splitThreadNetwork() async {
  final b = await _post('/thread/split', Uint8List(0),
      timeout: const Duration(seconds: 45), retryOnConnError: false);
  if (b == null) return null;
  try { return $proto.StatusResponse.fromBuffer(b); }
  on Exception catch (e) {
    debugPrint('FluxCoapService.splitThreadNetwork: $e');
    return null;
  }
}

/// Starts Thread 1.4 credential *sharing* (the SHARE side) — POST
/// /thread/epskc.

